1. High-Level Overview
This repository follows a modular Terraform design where:

Environments layer → Defines environment-specific configurations such as test, dev, and prod.
Modules layer → Contains reusable infrastructure components such as VPC, EC2, and GitLab architecture.
This approach enables:

Reusability
Scalability
Environment isolation
Consistent infrastructure provisioning
2. Repository Structure Explanation
Root Level
.gitlab-ci.yml
terraform/

.gitlab-ci.yml
The .gitlab-ci.yml file defines the CI/CD pipeline used to run Terraform commands:

terraform init
terraform validate
terraform plan
terraform apply

Terraform Apply – Manual Execution
terraform apply has intentionally been configured as a manual step.

Making terraform apply manual helps to:

Prevent accidental infrastructure changes.
Ensure the Terraform plan is reviewed before execution.
Provide an audit trail showing who triggered the apply.
Add a safety gate before making real infrastructure changes.
3. terraform/environments/
The environments directory contains environment-specific Terraform configurations.

terraform/environments/
├── README.md
