14. Troubleshooting Step 5 – AMI Issue Identified
Root Cause
The Terraform AMI variable was checked:

var.ami_id

Result:

ami-068ce9ce73029fefc

The AMI was then verified using:

aws ec2 describe-images \
  --image-ids ami-068ce9ce73029fefc \
  --region eu-central-1

Result:

{
  "Images": []
}

Conclusion
The AMI:

ami-068ce9ce73029fefc

did not exist in:

eu-central-1

This was the root cause of:

Error: collecting instance settings: empty result

15. Fix Applied
Step 1 – Retrieve a Valid Ubuntu AMI
The following AWS CLI command was used to retrieve valid Ubuntu AMIs:

aws ec2 describe-images \
  --owners 099720109477 \
  --filters "Name=name,Values=ubuntu/images/hvm-ssd-gp3/ubuntu-noble-24.04-amd64-server-*" \
  --query 'Images[*].[ImageId,Name]' \
  --region eu-central-1 \
  --output table

The selected valid AMI was:

ami-0b9870706bef68b28

Step 2 – Update Terraform Configuration
The AMI configuration was updated:

ami_id = "ami-0b9870706bef68b28"

The following option was also enabled:

use_existing_vpc = true

