23. Key Learnings
Invalid AMI IDs Can Cause Generic Terraform Errors
The Terraform error:

Error: collecting instance settings: empty result

can be caused by an invalid or unavailable AMI ID.

Always validate the AMI before deployment:

aws ec2 describe-images \
  --image-ids <AMI_ID> \
  --region <AWS_REGION>

For example:

aws ec2 describe-images \
  --image-ids ami-0b9870706bef68b28 \
  --region eu-central-1

Existing VPC Deployments
When deploying into an existing VPC, ensure:

use_existing_vpc = true

is configured where required.

Also verify:

VPC ID
Subnet IDs
Security group IDs
AWS region
Ubuntu AMI SSH Username
For Ubuntu AMIs, the default SSH username is:

ubuntu

Example:

ssh -i <key.pem> ubuntu@<private-ip>

Do not use:

ec2-user

for Ubuntu unless the image has been specifically configured with that user.

AWS Provider Errors
AWS provider errors can sometimes hide the actual EC2 validation failure.

When an error such as:

collecting instance settings: empty result

occurs, validate the underlying AWS resources independently using the AWS CLI.

Recommended checks include:

AMI
VPC
Subnet
Security Group
Key Pair
IAM Role
Region

